Implemented the FastAPI backend, API-specific SQLite helpers, role-scoped endpoints, magic-byte-checked uploads, audit logging, mock notifications/transfers, and the required TestClient flows. Added the one-line `web/index.html` placeholder and dependencies without changing the shared database schema or protected UI files. **Validation:** 8 tests passed; Uvicorn returned the static index and demo-account roles successfully. Starlette emitted an upstream TestClient/httpx deprecation warning. The worktree is clean; commits are `2c0fde0` and `a8c36b0` (not pushed). Git also printed a permission warning while cleaning metadata for another worktree, but both commits succeeded.

### ­şîÉ Community Wisdom
Only a few relevant posts surfaced, and the comment queries returned none, so these are practitioner pointers rather than broad consensus.

­şøí´©Å [[The security and quality checklist I use before launching a SaaS: multi-tenant isolation, role-based access, idempotency, audit logs](https://dev.to/mamareza/the-security-and-quality-checklist-i-use-before-launching-a-saas-multi-tenant-isolation-25b2)] ­şæñ [@mamareza](https://dev.to/mamareza) ÔÇö The post stresses checking role, ownership, guarded money-moving transitions, and auditability, which informed the APIÔÇÖs authorization and state-change handling. ­şöù [Read Full Discussion on DEV](https://dev.to/mamareza/the-security-and-quality-checklist-i-use-before-launching-a-saas-multi-tenant-isolation-25b2)

­şû╝´©Å [[Validating Image File Uploads in Ecommerce Chat Widgets to Prevent Security Risks](https://dev.to/romdevin/validating-image-file-uploads-in-ecommerce-chat-widgets-to-prevent-security-risks-1mec)] ­şæñ [@romdevin](https://dev.to/romdevin) ÔÇö Validating file signatures instead of trusting names or headers supports the upload endpointÔÇÖs content-based checks. ­şöù [Read Full Discussion on DEV](https://dev.to/romdevin/validating-image-file-uploads-in-ecommerce-chat-widgets-to-prevent-security-risks-1mec)

ÔÜÖ´©Å [[Testing FastAPI Endpoints Without Spinning Up a Server](https://dev.to/peytongreen_dev/testing-fastapi-endpoints-without-spinning-up-a-server-j74)] ­şæñ [@peytongreen_dev](https://dev.to/peytongreen_dev) ÔÇö In-process TestClient coverage is a practical fit for verifying routing and authorization without binding test ports. ­şöù [Read Full Discussion on DEV](https://dev.to/peytongreen_dev/testing-fastapi-endpoints-without-spinning-up-a-server-j74)

